[h1]R.A.T.S. Radio[/h1]
[i]R.A.T.S. – Reconnaissance, Acoustics, Terrain & Signals[/i]

[b]The radio net finally sounds like people.[/b]
43 voices instead of a screen reader, and your units tell you why they aren't doing what you ordered.

[quote]▶ [b]Requires[/b] a mod loader: [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3835527459]R.A.T.S. Keel[/url] or Anchor Chain, either one
▶ [b]Watch:[/b] [url=https://youtu.be/pGwOIPXckpY]the radio net in a mission[/url] (sound on)
✉ Bugs, ideas, questions: [url=https://hub.sewerlabs.dev/s/radio]R.A.T.S. feedback board[/url]
⭐ A favourite helps other captains find it[/quote]

[h2]✦ New in 1.5[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Moods.[/b] Stressed when a missile comes in, pleased after a splash, low when a contact is lost; off in Options > Audio
[*][b]Aircraft heading home turn yellow[/b] on the 3D globe too
[*][b]Runs on 0.9.1[/b] and the flat map (0.8.7)
[/list]

[h2]✦ Highlights[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]A crew with a face.[/b] 43 voices: American, Canadian, English, Scottish, Irish, Australian and New Zealand accents; every unit its own
[*][b]Accents follow the nation.[/b] Ship names and squadron words in their country's accent family
[*][b]Units explain refusals.[/b] "Negative, no radar lock", "Unable, target not in rear aspect", "Reloading, ready in four minutes"
[*][b]A net that behaves.[/b] Urgent calls cut in, "two, fox three", hiss, mic click and squelch
[*][b]Contact reports[/b] from the unit whose sensor found it, with the bearing; a raid is one call
[*][b]Air ops and rescue.[/b] Joker, bingo, fuel emergency; survivors in the water, pickup, delivered
[*][b]Clickable messages.[/b] A unit or track number moves the camera there
[*][b]Order queue (F8).[/b] The selected unit's queued attacks, each with its own delete button
[/list]

[h2]▶ Quick start[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe, and a mod loader if you have none (Keel above)
[*]Switch R.A.T.S. Radio on in Mods
[*]Start a mission and give an order: the answer comes on the radio
[/olist]
[list]
[*][b]Watch it:[/b] [url=https://youtu.be/pGwOIPXckpY]the radio net in a mission[/url]
[*][b]Settings:[/b] Options > Audio > Rats Radio; changes apply at once
[/list]

[h2]⚙ How the net behaves[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Stock lines replaced:[/b] acknowledgements, fox and missile away, splashes, hits, incoming, sonar, ROE; the unit that triggered it says it
[*][b]Callsigns:[/b] ships by name ("Iowa"), aircraft by squadron ("Lancer 3-2"), the rest NATO style ("Viper two-one")
[*][b]Replies first,[/b] old calls dropped: a late "copy" confuses more than none
[*][b]A fresh mix[/b] of voices every mission; a reload keeps them
[*][b]On the game's voice channel:[/b] its volume slider still works
[/list]

[h2]⚙ Units explain refusals[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Weapons:[/b] outside the envelope, can't reach, inside minimum range, seeker can't see it
[*][b]Sensors:[/b] no radar lock, sonar contact only, below the radar horizon, no line of sight
[*][b]Situation:[/b] too low, not in the firing arc, not cleared to engage, reloading, defending
[*][b]Dropped orders:[/b] "no sensor can see the target" when the game silently deletes one
[/list]

[h2]⚙ Voice packs and settings[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Per country[/b] in Options > Audio > Rats Radio > Voice packs; the 43 voices are NATO (English)
[*][b]More languages planned[/b] as their own Workshop items: Russian, then Spanish
[*][b]Options:[/b] female voices, random voices, static, volumes per call type, overlapping voices
[*][b]Squadron voices:[/b] [i]BepInEx\config\SeaPowerRadio\squadrons.txt[/i], e.g. [i]Bear Aces = female[/i]
[/list]

[h2]⚠ Good to know[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]About 910 MB[/b] of voices with their moods, no internet needed
[*][b]Other mods' voice lines[/b] play as before
[*][b]If a game update moves a hook,[/b] only that feature turns off and the log says which
[*][b]No game files are changed;[/b] every feature can be turned off
[/list]

[h2]⚙ Install and game versions[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Run in the game on 0.9.1[/b] (build 261112): Red Sea Breakout, under R.A.T.S. Keel
[*][b]0.8.7 (flat map):[/b] run there with earlier versions; the right build switches on by itself
[*][b]More:[/b] [url=https://github.com/struckl/SeaPowerRadio]README on GitHub[/url]
[/list]

